si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre cubrieron necesidades distintas de otros meses.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 123 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 32.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.8, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.0 to 4.8. December accounts for 7% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,896 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar proportions exist in all contracts. Having multiple contracts with the same provider does not prove wrongdoing, as it may reflect routine service needs.\nWhat can be checked: Check if December contracts are part of a larger pattern. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they align with standard service requirements. Contract [1] shows a single, small transaction that may reflect normal procurement practices.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["jjn%2FWKPHwKWExvMJXBMHHQ%3D%3D","vodGtTXBn09q1DdmE7eaXg%3D%3D","SG9fnl8V7dM%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}